{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/489241-2-attacks-per-round","id":489241,"title":"2 attacks per round?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-23T04:21:59-07:00","id":489241,"title":"2 attacks per round?","content":"Are there any merits/powers that allow you to do more than one attack per round?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1486-belladonna_izy","name":"Belladonna_izy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T04:24:46-07:00","id":489270,"title":"","content":"Not in 2nd edition. Multiple attacks(or actions in general) pretty quickly breaks the scope of this system's mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T06:53:03-07:00","id":489427,"title":"","content":"The fifth dot of the Relentless Assault fighting style lets you get a second attack if your first finishes your current target. <br /> <br /> Admittedly it's supposed to be for werewolves but I think a vampire (especially a gangrel) could use it without much issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T11:43:21-07:00","id":489710,"title":"","content":"The most common source of multiple actions in one turn are Merits that let you take a normally instant action as a reflexive one (Crack Driver, Parkour).<br /> <br /> Elfive has noted that only 2e instance of two attacks in a turn (though the drawback of it is fairly rough giving it sends you into instant Death Rage if you use it). So 2e doesn't seem like it will completely deny such things, but they're going to be far more costly than 1e when they come up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T15:59:02-07:00","id":489958,"title":"","content":"Anyhow, for 3 second rounds, asking for more than one attack is slightly ridiculous considering each of those attacks are abstract representations of actual combat. It's always something that needs to be explained to players, that &quot;1 attack&quot; isn't just one thrust of a blade, swing of an axe or bullet of a semi-automatic pistol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T21:17:55-07:00","id":490179,"title":"","content":"The system could use some adjustment to reinforce that particular point; especially as one firearms attack is just one bullet unless burst fire is applied in some fashion.<br /> <br /> Something that's come up in the past, is reducing the capacity of firearms in the system to make it clear that one fire arms attack isn't just one clean shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T00:43:58-07:00","id":490287,"title":"","content":"The one bullet thing kind of makes me think that it <i>is</i> one clean shot. <br /> <br /> Maybe firing wildly could be modelled as a kind of limited autofire, except it reduced the weapons damage rating because you're more likely to hit <i>something</i> but less likely to hit something <i>important. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T04:04:47-07:00","id":490397,"title":"","content":"Good riddance to multi-attack merits. I'm actually a bit annoyed they brought it back in Werewolf, and I hope that's the only instance that every has multiple attacks in 2e. Multi-attacks were terrible in the first place, and it would be even worse now, with how damage from weapons work. <br /> <br /> It created a situation in 1e where, if you weren't mastering a Fighting Style, you weren't fit for physical combat. It multiplied your power far more effectively than someone who never took one. Even beyond supernatural powers. It was even worse when it multiplied the two together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T04:15:10-07:00","id":490398,"title":"","content":"I think the idea is that you're not so much making multiple attacks as making one massive attack that cleaves through multiple opponents. Hence needing to lay out your primary target to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T11:13:40-07:00","id":490732,"title":"","content":"At least the werewolf one is more akin to a &quot;cleave&quot; (to borrow D&amp;D parlance a minute), so you don't really hit the same foe twice, plus the drawback is <i>extremely nasty</i> (Basu-Im immediately after).<br /> <br /> The Hurt Locker Notes thread contains some fighting styles/merits that trigger multiples attacks, except <i>not on the same opponent</i>. There is a staff one, for ex., doing a &quot;whirlwing&quot; attack move all around. I actually think if they keep it that way, it won't be so bad since it doesn't increase single target damage leading to insta-kills. Anyhow, the thread is still open for feedback, so I'd bring arguments there as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T11:23:00-07:00","id":490739,"title":"","content":"Death Rage isn't that nasty. If you're in a situation where you need to be killing people as fast as possible it's probably your best option. But it's definitely worse than Frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T12:26:02-07:00","id":490801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/489241-2-attacks-per-round?p=490732#post490732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hurt Locker Notes thread contains some fighting styles/merits that trigger multiples attacks, except <i>not on the same opponent</i>. There is a staff one, for ex., doing a &quot;whirlwing&quot; attack move all around. I actually think if they keep it that way, it won't be so bad since it doesn't increase single target damage leading to insta-kills. Anyhow, the thread is still open for feedback, so I'd bring arguments there as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also worth noting that you can do this without any Merits: It's how automatic firearms attacks (medium and full bursts anyway) already work. You spray bullets at a group of people and you roll for each one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/489241-2-attacks-per-round?p=490739#post490739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death Rage isn't that nasty. If you're in a situation where you need to be killing people as fast as possible it's probably your best option. But it's definitely worse than Frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>While automatic Basu-Im isn't the end of the world, and in a desperate situation might not be the worst idea, I can think of a lot of situations where a werewolf might want to be killing people as fast as possible; without wanting to deal with the issues that arise out of going into Basu-Im or the risk of sending their whole pack that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T03:52:07-07:00","id":491526,"title":"","content":"Do you know in 1e what merits/powers allowed multiattack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1486-belladonna_izy","name":"Belladonna_izy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T03:56:17-07:00","id":491527,"title":"","content":"It was the purview of fighting styles, mostly. Gunslinger, Two Weapons, Boxing, Kung Fu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T08:52:58-07:00","id":494872,"title":"","content":"Pretty much EVERY fighting style had at least one ability that would let you perform multiple attacks, usually at the cost of your Defense for the turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T15:29:14-07:00","id":496823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belladonna_izy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/489241-2-attacks-per-round?p=491526#post491526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know in 1e what merits/powers allowed multiattack?</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, the Kung Fu and Two Weapons Fighting Styles were the particularly notorious standouts as they were right there in the corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}